  "metaDescription": "The FSSAI has initiated a nationwide enforcement drive on packaged drinking water brands following the prosecution of Bisleri over an unsafe water sample.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The FSSAI has launched comprehensive, pan-India laboratory testing of packaged drinking water brands.",
    "The regulator initiated prosecution proceedings against Bisleri after a water sample from a Goa batch failed quality tests.",
    "Bisleri stated that the affected batch has been removed from circulation and noted that subsequent retests indicated bromate levels were within limits."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Food Safety and Standards Authority of India (FSSAI) has initiated a widespread enforcement operation targeting packaged drinking water manufacturers across the country. This regulatory action follows a specific incident in Goa where a batch of Bisleri water was found to be non-compliant during routine safety testing, leading authorities to sanction prosecution against the company. While the company maintains that the specific batch was withdrawn from the market and points to later internal or external retests showing levels within permitted limits, the FSSAI is now conducting a broader investigation. Regional agencies, such as the Goa Food and Drug Administration, have also intensified surveillance of various water brands. The results of the comprehensive, nationwide laboratory analysis are expected to be available within one to two months, as regulators aim to ensure compliance with national safety standards for bottled water.",
